A||N||4||Conrad Sanville||Alternator removal||||1||
Z||000000||Conrad Sanville||09-13-2000||10:07 PM||||<BR>I have to remove the alternator in my 85 2.5L. What is the easiest way? I've taken the alternator out of my GT through the bottom, the 2.5L looks like it is going to be tricky.  Any ideas?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Radcon||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||09-13-2000||11:43 PM||||<BR>I have not pulled an alternator off a 2.5 in a while, but the last time I did I pulled it thru the bottom.  Not too much work, just some contorsions.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000002||DjKid||09-13-2000||11:48 PM||||I've pulled mine in my 88 2.5l out the bottom and out the top.. ALOT easier out the top I must say, a few squezes by a few wires and a pipe and you're out. simple!<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe<BR><A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ralph||09-14-2000||04:44 AM||||Just pulled the alternator from my 87 4 cyl coupe yesterday. It came out the bottom real easy. I backed it onto ramps before I started. Pulled the oil filter to make access to the bottom bolt easier.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/yellowformula/LittleFiero.jpg"> <BR>  <B>  Ralph </B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Conrad Sanville||09-14-2000||07:03 AM||||Thanks for the advise. The alternator is one of a few repairs I have to perform on the 85 to put it back on the road for yet another winter. This is one of three white Fiero's I now own and have been driving these wonderful cars exclusively since 1983!  Thanks again.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Radcon||||reg||1
